<urn:atm:triage:finding/FNX-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FNX-003" ;
  triage:title "CDR-001 fix treats tasks_v2.revision as an authorization epoch, but audit writes bump it without changing authorization inputs" ;
  triage:description "fenix's independent critical review of PR #1395 confirms the CDR-001 race fix itself is correct (authorized_revision() binds mutation to the service-read row, CASed in the writer transaction, with a genuinely deterministic race test at herdr_queue_wake.rs:1223-1325). The gap: revision is now load-bearing as an authorization epoch, but record_reminder and record_lead_notified (task_reminder.rs:28-36,77-85) both UPDATE tasks_v2 SET revision = ? without touching current_assignee or current_attempt, and the attention scheduler emits these autonomously every TASK_REMINDER_INTERVAL_MS=60000 against every open task. A scheduler audit write landing inside the service's read-then-mutate window now makes an otherwise-authorized atm task start/block/unblock/complete fail ATM_TASK_REVISION_STALE with no automatic retry -- a new spurious-failure mode with no test and no doc. It also falsifies sprint-AZ.3-task-command-handoff.md:204-206's claim that authorization is 'rechecked against the current revision inside it', since a revision bump from an audit write does not correspond to an authorization-relevant change. Recommendation (preferred, smaller change): have RecordReminder/RecordLeadNotified not advance revision, since they already carry their own reminder_ordinal/last_reminded_at for staleness tracking -- so the counter means only 'authorization inputs may have changed'. Add a test that a reminder audit landing between authorization and mutation does not fail an authorized transition." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "concurrency-correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/task_command/service.rs, crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/task_reminder.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-10T19:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AZ.4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-10T19:42:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FNX-003/AZ4-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

